{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1153669-thunder-punch","id":1153669,"title":"Thunder Punch.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-27T21:53:14-07:00","id":1153669,"title":"Thunder Punch.","content":"On Page 422 in the MTA 20th anniversary book, there's a side bar which introduces this method, however it only seemed to explain hand to hand combat maneuvers and little to no information regarding gun play. What I wanted to ask is, can you take roughly the same concept and put it into another use? For example, using Correspondence 1 to spot the best spot to fire at with a firearm, or Entropy 1 to pick out the weakest spots or 2 to change the probability of the bullet striking some sort of softer tissue causing more damage, or life 1 in order to detect previous injures or the best spot to fire a gun for maximum damage, while system wise dropping the difficulty up to a maximum of three? Also, can this be used with duration added to it?<br /> <br /> Also, can you stack the difficulty reduction from the spell with other modifiers? For example, you get -3 from a casted effect as mentioned above and you attempt to get someone from behind, does it stack up to -5 difficulty or the maximum of -3?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12188-theexplosivearrow","user":"TheExplosiveArrow","date":". 10-28-2017, 12:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12188-theexplosivearrow","name":"TheExplosiveArrow","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-28T02:25:46-07:00","id":1153698,"title":"","content":"Sure, why not? As long as your Mage believes this is a thing they can do with a gun, and as long as it makes sense to them to use the spheres like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-28T03:15:48-07:00","id":1153702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheExplosiveArrow</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1153669-thunder-punch#post1153669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, can you stack the difficulty reduction from the spell with other modifiers? For example, you get -3 from a casted effect as mentioned above and you attempt to get someone from behind, does it stack up to -5 difficulty or the maximum of -3?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In my games, there is a lower difficulty limit of 3 and a maximum of 9 (using thresholds, if difficulty goes higher). Also -3 and +3 are the maximum modifiers when it comes to how a character can modify difficulty. The difficulty to attack from behind, however is described as beeing 4 in the rulebook, so modified with a spell it would be 3 instead.<br /> I feel this is a good enough system, it'd be kind of redundant rolling on difficulty 2 or 1, you could say they're basically automatic sucesses.<br /> <br /> For the spell effects: Yeah, totally do that. Mage rotes and spell descriptions are just examples to explain how the game works. You can go wyld!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","name":"TheVarulfen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-28T18:20:18-07:00","id":1153846,"title":"","content":"Page 414 has the violence enhancing magick and magick enhancing violence sections, which specifically included bullets.<br /> <br /> Thunder Punch is just a worked example of using a nonmagical combat attack with magick to do more damage.<br /> <br /> The rules on modifiers on page 503 make the maximum overall change from modifiers 3 points in either direction (+3 or -3) and the minimum difficulty is always 3.<br /> <br /> If you're using the violence first, then roll to see if you hit. If you hit, then the Arete roll can determine the additional damage. If you are using the violence as a focus for the damage, such as using Forces like a poltergeist to throw all the pots off the terraces onto your foe below, that's an Arete roll because the magick is the attack.<br /> <br /> You still have the limit of +3/-3 to modifiers, but a smart mage can do a lot of things when the difficulty is low.<br /> <br /> <i>Tales of Magick: Dark Adventure</i> had a lot of action movie stunts that while put into Mage 20, may not have as much detail as in the original source. In Mage, being creative is a good thing. Think of spheres as various threshold levels at each rank--rank 1 is notice and higher ranks let you manipulate more and more of that sphere in a nonlinear fashion.<br /> <br /> Life 1 is the least likely of the spheres suggested by the OP for enhancing combat, but figuring out where to target a wounded foe and then targeting that spot for maximum pain works well. Essentially, Life 1 would show you where to make the 'called shot.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-29T04:12:51-07:00","id":1153898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>baakyocalder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1153669-thunder-punch?p=1153846#post1153846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're using the violence first, then roll to see if you hit. If you hit, then the Arete roll can determine the <b>total</b> damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fixed that for you. Whenever Arete actually causes direct damage points in that section (As opposed to making things easer to hit, changing the damage type for the attack, making it harder to dodge, boosting attributes etc), it always causes the total damage, not additional damage.<br /> For example, if you shot a bullet and enhanced it by forces on impact, things like the normal weapon damage, the extra dice you get from a good hit, etc. all don't apply. You simply roll straight Arete for the total damage.<br /> <br /> And yes...this is nonsensical from a logic point of view. If the fiery forces effect fizzles out, the bullet does nothing at all, despite mundanely hitting.<br /> It's the aspect I reeeeeeaally don't like about that rule purely because logic, but it was done with balance in mind, I presume.<br /> The Arete damage scale is nasty good, especially with forces adding an automatic success on top. Add some quint and a willpower point success, and an Arete 3 roll has a good chance of doing 10 aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> This also gets re-iterated in the FAQ section of the Book Of Secrets:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In Such Situations, Does the Damage from<br /> the Effect \u201cStack\u201d Onto the Damage from the<br /> Mundane Attack?<br /> <br /> No. The Effect determines the damage \u2013 see Targeted<br /> Damage Effect under Examples in Play , Chapter Ten , p. 563 </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 10-29-2017, 07:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-29T15:53:05-07:00","id":1154007,"title":"","content":"Ah, missed the revision when replying. It's good to know, since I have a martial arts using PC with Forces 3 in my campaign.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}